WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Nitric acid is a strong acid.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.050
Methanoic acid is a weak one.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.370
A strong acid ionizes completely in water.

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.410
A weak acid ionizes only partly.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.130
So which acid has the lower pH?

6
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.150
Can a strong acid ever have
a higher pH than a weak acid?

7
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.050
In this mission, you'll find out
what makes an acid strong or weak,

8
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.750
and meet the strong acids
and bases you need to know.

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.170
You'll compare strong and weak
acids at equal concentration,

10
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.190
and work out which way an
acid–base equilibrium lies.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.270
Your mission:

12
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.610
decide whether a strong acid can ever
have a higher pH than a weak one.
